# Files carried into every worktree Claude Code creates (gitignore syntax; only files that match
# a pattern AND are gitignored are copied).
#
# This repo needs one because the directories that govern how work is done here are all
# git-ignored — `/.claude/` and `/.research/` in .gitignore. A worktree is a fresh checkout of
# *tracked* files, so without this file every subagent worktree starts without the locked
# decisions, the engineering standards, the reviewer agents, or the spec corpus, and re-derives
# them from whatever the spawning prompt happened to say. Four agents ran that way before this
# file existed.
#
# Patterns name the ignored directory directly rather than starting with `**/`, because a `**/`
# pattern only reaches inside a wholly-ignored directory when the first name after it is part of
# that directory's path.

# The rules a change is judged against, and the reviewers that judge it.
.claude/rules/**
.claude/agents/**
.claude/hooks/**
.claude/settings.json

# The spec corpus. Top level only: `.research/*.txt` is the corpus, everything below it is
# superpowers working state.
.research/*.txt

# Plans an agent may be executing. Specs and reports stay in the main checkout.
.research/superpowers/plans/**

# Skills, enumerated rather than globbed. `studio` is deliberately absent: its embedded book
# corpus is 103M, and a partial copy is worse than none, since its own SKILL.md requires every
# design decision to go through a search over that corpus. Run UI work from the main checkout.
.claude/skills/research/**
.claude/skills/testing/**
.claude/skills/scaffold-component/**
.claude/skills/keep-changelog/**
.claude/skills/readme-wizard/**
.claude/skills/graphify/**
.claude/skills/bun-docs/**
.claude/skills/bun-webview/**
.claude/skills/typescript-7/**
.claude/skills/react-router/**
.claude/skills/gh/**

# Deliberately NOT copied:
#
# `.env`             — a worktree that needs Vault credentials is doing integration work that
#                      belongs in the main checkout. Copying secrets widens where they sit on disk
#                      for the convenience of an agent that should not have them.
# `.graphify/`       — 6.8M, and a worktree does not need it. GRAPHIFY_OUT is now relative, so a
#                      worktree resolves it to its own (absent) directory and the guard exits
#                      silently rather than advising against a stale copy of the main graph.
# `node_modules/`    — worktrees live under `.claude/worktrees/` inside the repo, and Bun's
#                      resolution walks upward, so the root install already serves them. This is
#                      the same upward walk LD-14 records as defeating package isolation; here it
#                      happens to be the behaviour we want.
# `.claude/worktrees/` — copying it into a worktree would nest every existing worktree inside the
#                      new one.
